.\" Manpage for airpods-control.
.TH AIRPODS-CONTROL 1 "July 22, 2026" "airpods-control 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
airpods-control \- control AirPods listening mode and Conversation Awareness
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B airpods-control
.RB [ --device
.IR name ]
.RB ( listening-mode | lm )
.RB ( get | list )
.RB [ --json ]
.RB [ --debug ]
.br
.B airpods-control
.RB [ --device
.IR name ]
.RB ( listening-mode | lm )
.BI "set " mode
.RB [ --json ]
.RB [ --debug ]
.br
.B airpods-control
.RB [ --device
.IR name ]
.RB ( conversation-awareness | ca )
.B get
.RB [ --json ]
.RB [ --debug ]
.br
.B airpods-control
.RB [ --device
.IR name ]
.RB ( conversation-awareness | ca )
.BI "set " "on|off"
.RB [ --json ]
.RB [ --debug ]
.br
.B airpods-control
.RB [ --version | -v | version ]
.RB [ --help | -h ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B airpods-control
reads and sets the AirPods listening mode and Conversation Awareness by talking
directly to the macOS system audio daemon through a private AVFoundation API
.RB ( AVOutputDevice
in
.BR AVRouting.framework ).
A change takes effect immediately and shows the same on-screen banner as a stem
press. No Control Center, menu bar, or Accessibility permission is involved.
.PP
Reaching the API requires forging one private audio entitlement
.RB ( com.apple.avfoundation.allow-system-wide-context )
inside the
.B airpods-control
process via a small interpose library inserted with
.BR DYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES .
See the project README and SECURITY document for the full trust model.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS LISTENING MODE
.TP
.BR "listening-mode get" ", " "lm get"
Print the current listening mode.
.TP
.BR "listening-mode set " mode ", " "lm set " mode
Set the listening mode. If the mode is already active, prints
.B ok
without issuing a write. Otherwise prints
.B ok
on a verified change, or
.B no-op
if the requested write did not change the setting.
.TP
.BR "listening-mode list" ", " "lm list"
Print the comma-separated modes supported by the connected device in the
deterministic order documented under
.BR MODES .
.SS CONVERSATION AWARENESS
.TP
.BR "conversation-awareness get" ", " "ca get"
Print the current Conversation Awareness state as
.B on
or
.BR off .
.TP
.BR "conversation-awareness set " "on|off" ", " "ca set " "on|off"
Set Conversation Awareness. The setter is idempotent and uses the same
.B ok
and
.B no-op
contract as listening mode.
.SS GLOBAL
.TP
.BR --version ", " -v ", " version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR --help ", " -h
Print global or resource-specific usage and exit. Help may appear anywhere in
a command, takes precedence over all operations, and never accesses the device.
.SH MODES
.B off
(silent no-op on AirPods Pro),
.BR transparency ,
.BR adaptive ,
.BR noise-cancellation .
.PP
For input,
.B trans
aliases
.BR transparency ;
.B automatic
and
.B auto
alias
.BR adaptive ;
and
.B anc
and
.B nc
alias
.BR noise-cancellation .
Output always uses canonical names. There is no alias for
.BR off .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--device " name
Target a compatible output device using a case-insensitive exact name match.
The option is accepted anywhere in an operational command and may be supplied
once. It never falls back to another device. No match or multiple exact matches
produce
.BR no-device .
.TP
.B --json
Emit structured JSON instead of plain script-friendly output. Accepted anywhere
in an operational command or global version command. Every JSON response has a
.B result
field. Device operations also contain
.B device
and the command's resulting
.B listeningMode
or
.B conversationAwareness
state; unavailable values are JSON
.BR null .
The listening-mode list command additionally returns
.BR supportedListeningModes .
.TP
.B --debug
Emit diagnostic logs to stderr without changing stdout, JSON, or the exit code.
Diagnostics cover the entitlement bypass, framework and selector discovery,
device selection, raw state, capability checks, writes, and read-back attempts.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
No supported AirPods found as the current output device (no-device).
.TP
.B 2
Missing or malformed arguments (bad-args).
.TP
.B 3
A requested write did not change the setting (no-op).
.TP
.B 4
The mode or feature is not available on this device (unsupported).
.SH NOTES
On AirPods Pro,
.B off
(the Normal state) is a silent no-op: the API accepts it but the hardware does
not change.
.B airpods-control
verifies every change by reading it back and reports
.B no-op
(exit 3) rather than falsely claiming success. Use
.B transparency
for a "hear everything" mode.
.PP
This relies on a private API and targets macOS Tahoe (26); Apple may change it
in any update. The tool probes known shared-system-audio context selector
variants and checks every required selector before invocation. It fails safe
(reporting
.B unsupported
or
.BR no-device )
rather than crashing when selectors are missing.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project documentation: https://github.com/raulg/airpods-control-cli
